# Portfolio structure

This GitHub repo is a monorepo. The live site is the Vite app in `portfolio-website/`.

```
Portfolio/
├── AGENTS.md                 # Agent workflows
├── .cursor/rules/            # Cursor rules (keep these current)
├── .github/workflows/ci.yml                      # quality, Chromium Playwright, dependency review, Pages deploy on main
├── .github/workflows/dependabot-auto-merge.yml   # gh pr merge --auto --squash for Dependabot
├── .github/dependabot.yml                        # npm updates for portfolio-website
└── portfolio-website/        # React + TypeScript site + e2e tests
    ├── src/
    │   ├── app/              # App shell, home page, and router
    │   ├── features/         # Feature-owned components and styles
    │   ├── shared/           # Reusable UI, navigation, theme, and pages
    │   └── styles/           # Global styles
    ├── e2e/
    ├── .husky/pre-commit     # lint-staged: eslint --fix + prettier --write
    └── playwright.config.ts
```

- Do not put app source or Playwright specs at the repo root.
- Use feature-first organization in `src/features/`; keep feature-specific components with their feature.
- Put only genuinely reusable code in `src/shared/`, and app composition/routing in `src/app/`.
- Use kebab-case directories and PascalCase React component filenames.
- GitHub Pages `base` is `/Portfolio/` (`vite.config.ts` and React Router paths).
- The homepage contains About plus one-item previews for latest Experience, Project, and Blog content. Full collections live at `/Portfolio/experience`, `/Portfolio/projects`, and `/Portfolio/blogs`; individual posts remain under `/Portfolio/blogs/:blogId`. Navigation uses React Router links, not scroll anchors.
- Keep `package.json` dependencies limited to packages imported by the app or required as peers. Do not keep unused UI libraries “for later”.
- New packages should be sibling folders with their own README, then linked from the root README.
- GitHub Actions should use Node 24-compatible action majors (for example `actions/upload-artifact@v7`, not `v4`).
- CI quality checks belong in `.github/workflows/ci.yml`: ESLint, Prettier, TypeScript, cspell (British English on blog copy), Chromium Playwright (including axe WCAG 2.2 AA), then dependency review (`actions/dependency-review-action@v5`). Fail only on newly introduced GitHub advisories (`fail-on-severity: low`, runtime and development scopes). Deploy to GitHub Pages from that same workflow only after `quality`, `e2e`, and `dependency-review` pass on `main`.
- Skip dependency review only with `[skip dependency-review]` in the commit message or PR title/body. Do not use `[skip ci]`.
- When `main` is protected, required checks are `CI / quality`, `CI / e2e`, and `CI / dependency-review`. Do not require `CI / deploy`.
- Dependabot PRs (including majors) use `.github/workflows/dependabot-auto-merge.yml` with `gh pr merge --auto --squash`. GitHub merges after required checks on `main`. Do not require human reviews for this to work.
- Pre-commit uses Husky + lint-staged to auto-fix; CI must keep using check-only scripts (`lint:eslint`, `lint:format`, `lint:types`, `lint:spelling`).
- Prettier and ESLint cover the whole repo: `portfolio-website` plus root `README.md`, `AGENTS.md`, `.github/`, and `.cursor/`. Do not limit format scripts to `src/` only.
